# ========== Environment & Secrets (NEVER commit these) ==========
# NOTE: application-local.yml / application-dev.yml are NOT excluded - every service's local
# and dev profiles are checked in deliberately (see docs/microservices-contract.md) so any
# clone can `mvn spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=local` with zero setup. They hold
# only placeholder dev values (documented as such inline), never real secrets - those only
# ever come from env vars in application-prod.yml / application-staging.yml.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.prod
.env.staging
.env.dev
local.properties
settings.local.json

# ========== Database & Local Services ==========
# Anchored to repo root (leading /) - the earlier bare `data/` matched ANY directory named
# "data" anywhere in the tree, which silently excluded frontend/src/data/ (real source,
# imported by AddressStep.tsx/CommunityStep.tsx) from git entirely. Found via a fresh-clone
# build test: `git ls-files` had zero entries for that directory despite it existing on disk
# with real content, and a genuinely fresh checkout failed to compile without it.
/db/
/data/
/postgres/
/redis/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ========== Logs ==========
*.log
logs/
log/

